WEBVTT

00:00:07.970 --> 00:00:10.590
Wiping off my tears.

00:00:10.610 --> 00:00:13.300
I'm starting to run now

00:00:13.310 --> 00:00:18.560
Tomorrow I'll be born anew.

00:00:19.360 --> 00:00:24.370
How could "you always be my friend"?

00:00:24.380 --> 00:00:29.280
That person's word makes me more courageous.

00:00:29.290 --> 00:00:33.480
There are times when it's possible I will be depressed

00:00:34.710 --> 00:00:38.580
and there are times when things are delightful.

00:00:39.090 --> 00:00:45.170
I'll always be

00:00:46.130 --> 00:00:51.020
next to you.

00:00:53.260 --> 00:00:55.910
Smiling 100%

00:00:55.920 --> 00:00:59.450
Striking 100%

00:00:59.570 --> 00:01:03.640
I've come so far.

00:01:04.120 --> 00:01:06.560
Being 100% pure

00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:10.190
The things I want to tell you

00:01:10.200 --> 00:01:14.670
change to treasure completely.

00:01:14.680 --> 00:01:17.190
in the 100% case

00:01:17.210 --> 00:01:20.950
Even if it's a long distance,

00:01:20.960 --> 00:01:27.280
I'll still say I would meet you with the same feelings.

00:01:35.730 --> 00:01:39.590
Everyone, a new job has come to DDS.

00:01:40.320 --> 00:01:45.760
Those who step into the valley of the Hitobashira
shall face the wrath of Mayahime.

00:01:45.780 --> 00:01:47.430
Is this a threatening letter?

00:01:47.580 --> 00:01:48.800
Yes.

00:01:48.830 --> 00:01:52.890
This was sent to the politician Takatobi Katsugorou.

00:01:53.620 --> 00:01:58.860
There are many bad rumors about him and that dam he’s building.

00:01:59.460 --> 00:02:08.820
This letter was sent to his villa in Jinchuumura, where the dam is going to be built.

00:02:08.850 --> 00:02:15.580
Just in case anything happens, he’s asked us to send our detectives from DDS.

00:02:15.600 --> 00:02:20.090
It’s probably nothing. Nevertheless, I’d like you to check it out.

00:02:20.230 --> 00:02:21.290
Understood!

00:02:21.820 --> 00:02:24.380
They've al growns strong, haven’t they?

00:02:26.110 --> 00:02:32.390
After solving so many difficult cases together,
they are now showing confidence in their work.

00:02:33.330 --> 00:02:37.850
Katagiri-kun, when did you change the eraser in this room?

00:02:39.130 --> 00:02:41.310
I haven’t for a while.

00:02:47.130 --> 00:02:48.780
A-A bug!

00:02:48.800 --> 00:02:50.450
Even in a place like this.

00:02:50.470 --> 00:02:52.780
They heard what we said just now then, huh.

00:02:53.980 --> 00:02:57.290
Hongou-kun, go with them.

00:02:58.060 --> 00:02:59.170
Understood.

00:03:04.110 --> 00:03:08.880
Now that you mention it, ever since the time of Hongou-sensei's arrival,

00:03:08.910 --> 00:03:11.760
we have found evidence of Pluto inside DDS.

00:03:28.590 --> 00:03:32.160
What's Hongou doing here?

00:03:32.180 --> 00:03:36.120
Maybe we're still not trusted?

00:03:36.520 --> 00:03:40.120
Is there some hidden aspect to this case?

00:03:40.520 --> 00:03:44.840
By the way, what was that “Hitobashira” in that letter?

00:03:44.860 --> 00:03:46.090
I looked it up.

00:03:46.820 --> 00:03:50.590
In ancient times, whenever people had difficulty during construction,

00:03:50.620 --> 00:03:53.930
it was their belief that the gods of the land were cursing them.

00:03:53.950 --> 00:03:57.720
And you know what they did to rid themselves of this curse?

00:03:57.750 --> 00:03:59.060
W-What?

00:04:00.920 --> 00:04:03.270
They made sacrifices.

00:04:03.290 --> 00:04:07.030
They'd tie people to a foundation pillar and bury them.

00:04:07.590 --> 00:04:10.070
§o that’s why they call it a Hitobashira.

00:04:10.090 --> 00:04:11.990
They bury them while still alive?

00:04:13.010 --> 00:04:16.790
For ages, Jinchuumura has suffered from bad floods

00:04:16.810 --> 00:04:19.450
They would give a sacrifice to their gods each
time a new building was constructed.

00:04:20.310 --> 00:04:25.460
It is said that the village’s tradition of Hitobashira
began with the legend of Mayahime.

00:04:26.150 --> 00:04:31.090
Whenever there was a great storm, a beautiful
woman named Mayahime would change herself.

00:04:31.110 --> 00:04:36.890
She would turn into a flaming dragon and
stop the flood with ash from her body.

00:04:36.910 --> 00:04:41.640
So until just a short while ago, the characters
“jin” and “chuu” in the village’s name,

00:04:41.670 --> 00:04:45.110
were written with the characters meaning “Hitobashira”

00:04:45.840 --> 00:04:47.570
That’s enough rambling.

00:04:47.590 --> 00:04:49.070
We're almost there.

00:04:49.090 --> 00:04:50.570
wo
$f

00:04:54.140 --> 00:04:54.360
we.

00:05:01.020 --> 00:05:03.370
It looks like a ghost town.

00:05:03.400 --> 00:05:07.460
Of course it does. This town will soon be submerged underwater.

00:05:07.480 --> 00:05:09.500
Where’s the inn?

00:05:13.660 --> 00:05:14.430
Hey!

00:05:14.450 --> 00:05:15.010
You!

00:05:16.990 --> 00:05:18.390
Why'd you throw that rock at me?

00:05:18.790 --> 00:05:20.850
That would’ve hurt if it had hit!

00:05:25.000 --> 00:05:26.730
You guys are with that evil politician, right?

00:05:27.750 --> 00:05:32.110
He’s trying to turn our village into the bottom of a lake!

00:05:32.630 --> 00:05:34.070
top it, Musashi-kun,

00:05:36.430 --> 00:05:37.760
Natsumi-neechan...

00:05:38.420 --> 00:05:42.160
You’re the detectives from Tokyo that Takatobi-sensei sent for, aren’t you?

00:05:42.850 --> 00:05:44.370
We're DDS.

00:05:44.400 --> 00:05:46.120
We've been waiting for you .

00:05:46.150 --> 00:05:48.330
l am the landlady of the inn.

00:05:48.360 --> 00:05:51.210
His secretaries are waiting for you.

00:05:51.240 --> 00:05:52.340
Please come this way.

00:05:51.650 --> 00:05:53.090
Please come this ways

00:05:53.150 --> 00:05:54.170
Yes.

00:05:55.530 --> 00:05:57.050
Traitor!

00:05:57.280 --> 00:06:00.350
This pace seems really tense.

00:06:01.580 --> 00:06:07.940
There are probably both people who oppose and
support the construction of the dam here.

00:06:07.960 --> 00:06:11.320
Diet Member Takatobi is supposedly a very pushy politician.

00:06:11.880 --> 00:06:16.950
Does it mean she supports him? She is letting his party rest at her inn.

00:06:17.390 --> 00:06:24.660
But there’s no doubt that somebody in this
village sent that letter threatening him.

00:06:25.310 --> 00:06:27.620
I've brought the DDS members.

00:06:27.940 --> 00:06:29.080
Thank you.

00:06:29.110 --> 00:06:29.920
Then I'll be going.

00:06:29.940 --> 00:06:32.590
Thank you for coming all this way.

00:06:33.150 --> 00:06:37.090
I am Takatobi’s second secretary, Hitsuki Yuri.

00:06:37.660 --> 00:06:38.760
We are DDS.

00:06:39.330 --> 00:06:41.050
Let me introduce you.

00:06:41.080 --> 00:06:43.220
This is Obana, the first secretary

00:06:43.500 --> 00:06:44.770
A pleasure.

00:06:44.790 --> 00:06:49.900
Thank you for coming al this way

00:06:49.920 --> 00:06:53.820
Thank you for coming.

00:06:53.830 --> 00:06:55.990
Kagaki Construction. My name’s Goura.

00:06:56.800 --> 00:06:58.490
My name is Hongou.

00:06:58.510 --> 00:07:02.950
My, my, my! These other detectives are quite young though.

00:07:02.970 --> 00:07:07.370
Is he perhaps an elementary schooler?

00:07:07.390 --> 00:07:11.750
If You're worried, I'll give you a little performance.

00:07:15.990 --> 00:07:19.090
Kagaki Construction has a 300 million yen in available capital,

00:07:19.110 --> 00:07:21.340
and 180 workers.

00:07:21.370 --> 00:07:23.850
A relatively large portion of its projects are for public works,

00:07:23.870 --> 00:07:25.390
and over half the company’s officers are former government officials.

00:07:26.370 --> 00:07:31.060
As for this Jinchuumura dam operation...

00:07:31.090 --> 00:07:34.320
Wow, that’s quite a high bid.

00:07:34.340 --> 00:07:36.860
I’m impressed that you got your bid accepted!

00:07:36.880 --> 00:07:38.440
Uh, I get it.

00:07:38.470 --> 00:07:41.200
Narusawa, that’s enough.

00:07:41.220 --> 00:07:42.070
Yes.

00:07:42.510 --> 00:07:47.910
All right then, I'll take you to the Diet Member's villa.

00:07:47.940 --> 00:07:49.660
Y Yes...

00:07:49.690 --> 00:07:51.670
Hitsuki-kun, get the car ready.

00:07:51.690 --> 00:07:52.630
Yes!

00:07:52.650 --> 00:07:54.090
Excuse me.

00:07:56.490 --> 00:08:00.170
Would you sign the inn’s register?

00:08:00.200 --> 00:08:01.220
Understood.

00:08:01.910 --> 00:08:05.600
Put your luggage in your room and prepare to depart.

00:08:05.620 --> 00:08:06.390
Yes.

00:08:07.330 --> 00:08:09.600
Hey Kazuma, that was a bit much.

00:08:09.620 --> 00:08:13.020
They're the client, isn’t it bad to talk down to them?

00:08:13.040 --> 00:08:19.690
I don’t care. Even Dan-sensei is aware of the corruption involved in this case.

00:08:19.720 --> 00:08:23.700
Well, that was quite a performance just now!

00:08:24.390 --> 00:08:25.280
You're. . .

00:08:25.310 --> 00:08:26.740
Oh, I’m sorry.

00:08:26.770 --> 00:08:27.950
I’m Jinnai.

00:08:27.980 --> 00:08:29.200
Nice ta meet’cha.

00:08:29.230 --> 00:08:30.660
A freelance journalist.

00:08:31.230 --> 00:08:34.420
I’m investigating this place as well.

00:08:34.440 --> 00:08:39.630
Well, I won't bother you, so share any info you get with me.

00:08:40.280 --> 00:08:44.140
In exchange, I'll tell you what I know.

00:08:45.280 --> 00:08:46.890
Unfortunately we can’t—

00:08:47.120 --> 00:08:48.140
“Understood!

00:08:48.160 --> 00:08:49.390
I accept!

00:08:49.540 --> 00:08:50.100
Kyuu!

00:08:50.790 --> 00:08:54.480
And in exchange, since it was your idea, you tell us first.

00:08:56.340 --> 00:08:58.610
Hey, I like you!

00:08:58.630 --> 00:09:00.320
You’re an interesting kid!

00:09:01.590 --> 00:09:02.570
I get that a lot!

00:09:04.350 --> 00:09:07.950
That naivety may be Kyuu’s greatest weapon.

00:09:07.970 --> 00:09:09.990
I think he’s just a snotty kid.

00:09:10.680 --> 00:09:14.620
First, the young landlady here named Mozu Natsumi:

00:09:14.650 --> 00:09:19.460
her father died five years ago when constructing a dam.

00:09:19.490 --> 00:09:23.590
On the surface, she's being hospitable to his party,

00:09:23.610 --> 00:09:26.760
but I’m wondering if she actually hates him enough to want to kill him

00:09:29.160 --> 00:09:34.770
That dam project was basically forced through
by Takatobi and Kagaki Construction.

00:09:35.330 --> 00:09:39.400
Then that “Musashi” kid who was all mad at us...

00:09:39.420 --> 00:09:40.530
What?

00:09:40.550 --> 00:09:43.070
You came under attack from him already?

00:09:43.090 --> 00:09:47.490
Well, his brother was killed by Takatobi and his gang.

00:09:48.350 --> 00:09:53.450
He’s seriously ready to stop the project at any cost.

00:09:53.810 --> 00:09:56.580
Dammit, don’t tell them that, you hyena!

00:09:56.610 --> 00:09:58.920
Heh, speak of the devil.

00:09:59.690 --> 00:10:02.630
What would my brother say if he saw you now?

00:10:05.660 --> 00:10:07.300
There you are...

00:10:07.320 --> 00:10:10.390
Everyone, the car is ready.

00:10:10.410 --> 00:10:11.720
Musashi-kun?

00:10:11.750 --> 00:10:13.100
You’re still here?

00:10:13.120 --> 00:10:14.560
Get out!

00:10:15.170 --> 00:10:20.020
If you don’t, the cursed flames of Mayahime’s Hitobashira will destroy you.

00:10:20.840 --> 00:10:23.190
The cursed flames of Hitobashira...

00:10:23.220 --> 00:10:27.280
Now it’s your turn, tell me what you know.

00:10:27.300 --> 00:10:31.370
Our investigations are kept secret, we can’t tell you anything.

00:10:31.390 --> 00:10:31.910
Let’s go!

00:10:31.930 --> 00:10:32.620
Right!

00:10:32.640 --> 00:10:33.540
Hey, wait a sec...

00:10:39.190 --> 00:10:41.790
We re gong pretty far.

00:10:55.000 --> 00:10:56.850
Then his villa?

00:10:56.870 --> 00:10:57.690
That!

00:11:00.130 --> 00:11:01.150
et?

00:11:03.960 --> 00:11:07.110
Isn’t that a warehouse?

00:11:07.130 --> 00:11:09.240
It's made out of concrete blocks:

00:11:09.260 --> 00:11:11.870
No, that’s just how he likes it,

00:11:12.180 --> 00:11:13.620
How he likes it?

00:11:13.640 --> 00:11:15.290
I see...

00:11:15.310 --> 00:11:19.620
When a dam is built, anybody forced to move is given compensation.

00:11:19.650 --> 00:11:23.210
He built that here just for the compensation?

00:11:23.230 --> 00:11:25.050
And that means that even if he gets a threatening letter,

00:11:25.070 --> 00:11:27.510
he can’t move, since he won’t get the compensation.

00:11:27.990 --> 00:11:30.510
And he’s the driving force behind the dam’s construction.

00:11:30.530 --> 00:11:31.680
Impressive.

00:11:31.700 --> 00:11:34.310
Dammit. That pisses me off.

00:11:40.880 --> 00:11:41.940
What's wrong, Kyuu?

00:11:44.510 --> 00:11:45.360
Look!

00:11:45.380 --> 00:11:46.360
A grasshopper!

00:11:48.050 --> 00:11:48.950
You idiot!

00:11:51.760 --> 00:11:54.280
Hey, that villas a bit weird.

00:11:54.310 --> 00:11:54.700
What?

00:11:54.720 --> 00:11:55.280
Where?

00:11:56.350 --> 00:12:01.290
The area around the fan above the door: it’s covered in soot.

00:12:01.730 --> 00:12:02.920
You're right!

00:12:02.940 --> 00:12:04.090
That’s.

00:12:04.110 --> 00:12:05.670
No way a fire?

00:12:05.690 --> 00:12:07.380
Oh no!

00:12:08.740 --> 00:12:11.130
Sensei!

00:12:11.160 --> 00:12:13.930
There’s no response! Where is he?

00:12:13.950 --> 00:12:14.720
Where’s the key for this?

00:12:15.370 --> 00:12:20.560
It’s not locked, but there’s something holding it from the inside.

00:12:20.580 --> 00:12:22.020
Both of you get-out of the way.

00:12:22.040 --> 00:12:23.560
Touyama, we're going to ram it.

00:12:23.590 --> 00:12:24.190
Right!

00:12:28.720 --> 00:12:29.740
Dammit.

00:12:29.760 --> 00:12:31.450
It’s no good, it won’t open.

00:12:32.640 --> 00:12:35.320
Touyama, can you operate that power shovel?

00:12:35.850 --> 00:12:36.450
Of course!

00:12:40.850 --> 00:12:43.370
I didn't get a part-time job at a construct on site for nothing!

00:12:47.730 --> 00:12:53.050
This is one of the concrete blocks we saw stacked at the materials site!

00:12:53.620 --> 00:12:57.510
With something like this in front of the door, there’s no way it could open

00:12:57.910 --> 00:12:59.930
What the hell is that doing here?

00:13:02.580 --> 00:13:04.350
Ryuu, what’s wrong?

00:13:08.340 --> 00:13:10.230
Takatobi-sensei!

00:13:12.970 --> 00:13:14.240
The curse of...

00:13:16.760 --> 00:13:18.240
Mayahime’s Hitobashira!

00:13:30.900 --> 00:13:33.090
The window’s locked too.

00:13:33.110 --> 00:13:34.590
And these are iron bars!

00:13:35.240 --> 00:13:40.060
The fan’s pretty large, but there’s no room
for more than an arm to pass through.

00:13:40.660 --> 00:13:45.650
Wait, the door was blocked with a concrete block from inside.

00:13:45.670 --> 00:13:48.110
It's impossible to go in and out.

00:13:48.130 --> 00:13:51.570
Does that mean he locked himself in and burned himself to death?

00:13:52.260 --> 00:13:53.860
No, it doesn’t.

00:13:55.840 --> 00:14:00.080
There’s no ash inside the nose or mouth at all.

00:14:00.100 --> 00:14:03.540
That means he was burned after he died.

00:14:04.350 --> 00:14:07.250
The evidence is shown by these marks on his neck,

00:14:08.400 --> 00:14:10.590
These marks are made when being strangled.

00:14:10.610 --> 00:14:13.170
Then, this is a locked room murder.

00:14:14.150 --> 00:14:19.680
And the locked room is so perfect that a crime is impossible!

00:14:27.670 --> 00:14:29.310
A locked room murder.

00:14:30.130 --> 00:14:31.770
Look at this.

00:14:32.420 --> 00:14:35.190
This is how things appeared in the crime scene as we entered.

00:14:37.050 --> 00:14:40.070
A child’s opinion is rather unreliable.

00:14:40.100 --> 00:14:44.200
Sure you haven’t missed something? Like a concealed exit?

00:14:44.230 --> 00:14:46.040
There wasn’t!

00:14:46.060 --> 00:14:49.040
We searched it thoroughly,

00:14:49.060 --> 00:14:50.750
right Hongou-sensei?

00:14:50.770 --> 00:14:53.880
Then there’s only one answer.

00:14:53.900 --> 00:14:54.920
What do you mean?

00:14:55.700 --> 00:14:59.300
Diet Member Takatobi killed himself in this room.

00:14:59.700 --> 00:15:01.720
Suicide?

00:15:01.740 --> 00:15:03.060
No way.

00:15:03.080 --> 00:15:05.100
He’d never do that

00:15:05.120 --> 00:15:07.270
That can’t be true!

00:15:07.960 --> 00:15:09.730
Wait a moment.

00:15:09.750 --> 00:15:13.820
I think if's too teary to cal it a suicide.

00:15:15.470 --> 00:15:22.870
We know all about the famous detective,
Dan Morihiko, but you’re still apprentices.

00:15:22.890 --> 00:15:25.490
Your intuition alone isn’t enough.

00:15:26.020 --> 00:15:28.410
What are you teaching these kids?

00:15:29.230 --> 00:15:33.710
Detective, there are still many strange things about this crime scene.

00:15:34.650 --> 00:15:36.050
Like this.

00:15:36.070 --> 00:15:39.430
This is the same kind of block that was in front of the door.

00:15:40.030 --> 00:15:43.890
Could one of you try carrying it?

00:15:49.580 --> 00:15:51.600
One person couldn't possibly carry this.

00:15:51.630 --> 00:15:52.360
Hey.

00:15:52.540 --> 00:15:53.730
One two...

00:16:00.050 --> 00:16:01.360
It’s no good.

00:16:01.390 --> 00:16:02.780
We can’t pick it up.

00:16:03.680 --> 00:16:11.460
There’s no way that one skinny politician could
move that concrete block himself, is there?

00:16:11.480 --> 00:16:12.790
If it was suicide,

00:16:13.820 --> 00:16:18.380
then the victim would have carried the block inside

00:16:18.400 --> 00:16:22.260
and placed it in front of the door.

00:16:23.160 --> 00:16:25.260
That’s impossible.

00:16:25.290 --> 00:16:30.060
For one thing, he had no reason to commit a locked-room suicide.

00:16:30.080 --> 00:16:33.480
Then if it was a murder, then how did they kill him?

00:16:33.960 --> 00:16:35.860
We don’t know.

00:16:35.880 --> 00:16:40.950
But this case won't be resolved until we solve the mystery of the locked room.

00:16:41.720 --> 00:16:44.740
I think that’s certain.

00:16:47.470 --> 00:16:49.450
All right!

00:16:53.400 --> 00:16:55.790
What a great hot spring!

00:16:55.820 --> 00:16:57.460
Paradise! Paradise!

00:16:57.480 --> 00:17:00.760
Hot springs after you’ve used your head are the best!

00:17:00.780 --> 00:17:05.300
Hey Kyuu! Don’t just jump in here when other people are using it!

00:17:05.330 --> 00:17:07.100
My glasses got wet.

00:17:07.950 --> 00:17:13.690
But I wish Hongou would’ve covered for us a bit more.

00:17:13.710 --> 00:17:14.940
That’s right.

00:17:14.960 --> 00:17:18.520
Right after we got back, he went to his room and hid.

00:17:20.840 --> 00:17:22.570
This is quite a nice hot spring.

00:17:24.430 --> 00:17:26.530
How does the water feel?

00:17:26.850 --> 00:17:29.830
Ryuu, you look surprisingly sexy.

00:17:30.390 --> 00:17:34.870
Now that you mention it, this is the first time
you've been in a bath with the rest of us.

00:17:34.900 --> 00:17:35.790
Yeah.

00:17:35.810 --> 00:17:37.500
Is that so?

00:17:37.820 --> 00:17:43.380
But since there’s only guys here, you don’t need your towel!

00:17:43.410 --> 00:17:45.590
Hey, what are you doing?? Kinta!

00:17:45.620 --> 00:17:46.680
What?

00:17:46.700 --> 00:17:48.400
You lack self-confidence?

00:17:48.400 --> 00:17:50.850
Kinta, stop it. It’s dangerous!

00:17:50.870 --> 00:17:53.930
Wow, this is a really nice hot spring!

00:17:53.960 --> 00:17:55.020
Yuri-san!

00:17:55.040 --> 00:18:00.070
Indeed, the temperature is lower than usual, but nonetheless, it is a hot spring.

00:18:00.380 --> 00:18:02.490
Those voices... Megu, and ...

00:18:02.510 --> 00:18:06.360
That really hot politician’s secretary, Hitsuki Yuri-san.

00:18:08.140 --> 00:18:09.450
Hey, let’s go, Kyuu!

00:18:09.970 --> 00:18:11.290
Go? Where?

00:18:11.310 --> 00:18:12.540
It should be obvious.

00:18:16.100 --> 00:18:19.000
We're going to take a quick look at the paradise other the wall.

00:18:20.320 --> 00:18:21.960
S-Stop it, Kinta.

00:18:21.990 --> 00:18:23.920
Peeking is a crime!

00:18:23.950 --> 00:18:25.840
Don’t be so stuck-up, Ryuu.

00:18:25.860 --> 00:18:28.680
This is excellent opportunity to strengthen our male bonds!

00:18:29.450 --> 00:18:34.140
I’m fine. I'm young enough to go into a women’s bath anyways.

00:18:34.330 --> 00:18:36.440
Ignore the kiddy.

00:18:36.460 --> 00:18:39.230
Come on, Kyuu, you going or not?

00:18:41.630 --> 00:18:44.740
What are you doing, Kinta... I'll leave you here!

00:18:44.760 --> 00:18:47.200
You're surprisingly into It.

00:18:47.930 --> 00:18:50.370
Cheer up, Yuri-san.

00:18:50.390 --> 00:18:53.040
It’s not like it’s your fault,

00:18:53.060 --> 00:18:55.040
and we'll be sure to find the criminal.

00:18:55.690 --> 00:18:57.160
That’s not it.

00:18:57.600 --> 00:18:59.290
I’m scared.

00:19:00.570 --> 00:19:03.170
The next victim may be me.

00:19:05.110 --> 00:19:10.390
Regardless of whether this is a curse or a murder, the reason is the same.

00:19:10.580 --> 00:19:13.970
It was Kagaki Construction and Takatobi-sensei.

00:19:14.000 --> 00:19:16.930
who wanted to turn the village into the bottom of a lake.

00:19:16.960 --> 00:19:21.310
So then, why would you be killed?

00:19:22.250 --> 00:19:23.360
Because...

00:19:34.520 --> 00:19:37.710
I am a traitor.

00:19:41.190 --> 00:19:43.210
“Traitor”?

00:19:46.700 --> 00:19:48.170
Natsumi-chan, wait!

00:19:48.990 --> 00:19:54.140
Natsumi-chan, do you think I’m a traitor too?

00:19:54.580 --> 00:19:59.100
Not really. I don’t have any attachment to this village.

00:19:59.420 --> 00:20:03.190
If that’s what you mean, I may be a traitor too.

00:20:17.310 --> 00:20:19.040
Traitor huh?

00:20:19.770 --> 00:20:23.040
That Musashi kid spoke of it too.

00:20:23.900 --> 00:20:25.630
What does it mean, I wonder.

00:20:25.650 --> 00:20:28.510
Yeah, I dunno...

00:20:28.530 --> 00:20:30.380
I said I don’t

00:20:32.780 --> 00:20:34.090
Kinta, what do you think?

00:20:34.120 --> 00:20:35.510
<i>I-Idiot!</i>

00:20:42.540 --> 00:20:43.150
Idiot!

00:20:43.170 --> 00:20:43.600
Jerk!

00:20:43.630 --> 00:20:44.270
Pervert!

00:20:44.670 --> 00:20:47.440
It hurts!

00:20:47.460 --> 00:20:49.610
Gimmie a break, Megu!

00:20:49.630 --> 00:20:53.700
We were just playing and you really hurt us!

00:20:53.720 --> 00:20:57.700
Any further and it would’ve turned into the “Hot Springs Murders”!

00:20:57.720 --> 00:21:00.040
Want me to re-enact it?

00:21:01.650 --> 00:21:03.500
Kinta needs to learn, doesn’t he?

00:21:04.610 --> 00:21:07.500
You too, Kyuu!

00:21:07.530 --> 00:21:08.500
Sorry.

00:21:08.860 --> 00:21:10.550
You just don’t listen.

00:21:10.570 --> 00:21:12.930
Well guess you got what you deserved.

00:21:12.950 --> 00:21:14.010
Foolish.

00:21:18.160 --> 00:21:24.560
But now that Takatobi-sensei’s dead,
we'd better hurry and complete the dam.

00:21:24.580 --> 00:21:28.860
Anyway, it'll probably be the first secretary,
Obana, who inherits this district;

00:21:28.880 --> 00:21:30.900
so I gotta remember to be good to him.

00:21:31.720 --> 00:21:34.320
Take the next good deal to him.

00:21:39.890 --> 00:21:42.910
why would she call herself a traitor?

00:21:42.940 --> 00:21:44.250
Right?

00:21:44.270 --> 00:21:50.840
And she was really worried that she might end up being the next Hitobashira.

00:21:50.860 --> 00:21:55.260
Do you suppose, she’s from this village?

00:21:56.530 --> 00:22:00.930
Because that Musashi guy seemed to know her.

00:22:00.950 --> 00:22:04.770
“Traitor” seems to point towards them being together at some point.

00:22:05.290 --> 00:22:06.690
I see what you mean.

00:22:06.710 --> 00:22:09.770
If we think of this backwards, it makes sense.

00:22:09.800 --> 00:22:14.240
Takatobi brought her, young and inexperienced as fils secretary.

00:22:14.760 --> 00:22:16.240
Oh,

00:22:16.340 --> 00:22:19.580
it's you Natsumi san?

00:22:20.470 --> 00:22:22.160
You have a fax.

00:22:25.060 --> 00:22:28.250
I’m about to close them.

00:22:28.270 --> 00:22:32.500
Oh, I'll go in as soon as I look though these documents.

00:22:32.530 --> 00:22:35.220
All right, but please make haste lest the water become cold.

00:22:40.200 --> 00:22:42.970
Just walking into people’s rooms. . .

00:22:43.000 --> 00:22:45.680
This is why I hate the countryside.

00:22:45.710 --> 00:22:46.390
I was sure it was—

00:22:46.880 --> 00:22:49.060
Nah, I’m thinking too much.

00:22:57.640 --> 00:23:01.410
I’m sure this wasn’t a suicide.

00:23:02.020 --> 00:23:03.620
I agree.

00:23:03.640 --> 00:23:08.870
That confined room was something the criminal
constructed to make it appear to be a suicide.

00:23:08.900 --> 00:23:14.130
But the body didn’t burn as well as they thought,
which left behind evidence of the strangling.

00:23:14.530 --> 00:23:15.550
Yeah.

00:23:15.570 --> 00:23:17.630
This is not a curse or a suicide.

00:23:25.410 --> 00:23:31.310
The criminal used a trick we've never seen
before to create the locked room murder!

00:23:39.340 --> 00:23:41.490
This is clearly a premeditated murder!

00:23:47.860 --> 00:23:51.770
Somehow it's collapsing

00:23:51.800 --> 00:23:54.140
Embracing such a feeling.

00:23:54.160 --> 00:23:55.030
Flowing.

00:23:55.050 --> 00:23:58.910
I'd be worried tomorrow.

00:23:58.930 --> 00:24:01.120
If the same thing happened.

00:24:01.140 --> 00:24:02.120
Go wrong.

00:24:02.130 --> 00:24:06.460
He looks up at the sky, pondering

00:24:06.470 --> 00:24:09.020
You're very far away.

00:24:09.930 --> 00:24:13.180
Show your heart if you have the courage

00:24:13.190 --> 00:24:16.310
passing the border line.

00:24:16.330 --> 00:24:19.760
In order to get past, I walk against the wind

00:24:19.770 --> 00:24:23.400
and I can finish a battle.

00:24:23.420 --> 00:24:26.940
When I feel like an abandoned child

00:24:26.970 --> 00:24:30.360
then I'll stand in line with you.

00:24:30.390 --> 00:24:33.930
Facing the wind, I forget,

00:24:33.940 --> 00:24:37.540
somehow this is the only important thing.

00:24:37.550 --> 00:24:40.290
We protect, because there Is no return.

00:24:40.310 --> 00:24:41.890
It's becoming dearly.

00:24:41.920 --> 00:24:45.840
Today I embrace, right now I conquer.

00:24:47.070 --> 00:24:56.060
Next Episode

00:24:47.450 --> 00:24:50.230
The police decide that the crime is a suicide.

00:24:50.420 --> 00:24:53.190
At this rate we're going to fall into the criminal’s clever trap.

00:24:54.500 --> 00:24:57.400
A traitor amidst the opposing members of the village.

00:24:57.880 --> 00:24:59.570
The few clues left at the crime scene.

00:25:00.760 --> 00:25:04.030
Can DDS reveal the true nature of Mayahime’s curse?

00:25:04.350 --> 00:25:06.700
There’s one answer!

00:25:07.020 --> 00:25:10.700
By the way Kinta, did you get to see what you were looking for?

00:25:10.940 --> 00:25:15.210
Well, I went to see Hitsuki-san and all there was was Megu.

00:25:15.820 --> 00:25:18.380
I got beat up for nothing.
